docs {
  # Queue Management Tests
  
  Tests for queue creation and operation APIs.
  
  ## What Are Queues?
  
  Queues store messages for asynchronous processing. Each queue has:
  - Owner environment ID
  - Queue name
  - Zone and context
  - Queue type (CONSUMER, PROVIDER, SUBSCRIPTION)
  - Message storage (Redis + S3)
  
  ## Tests Included
  
  - Create queue
  - List queues
  - Get queue by ID
  - Enqueue message
  - Dequeue/poll message
  - Peek at messages
  - Acknowledge message
  - Delete queue
  - Error scenarios
  
  ## Important Notes
  
  - Queues require authentication
  - Messages persist to S3 before success is returned
  - Unacknowledged messages are redelivered
  - Queues are automatically created for DELAYED pattern requests
}
